---
import Base from "#src/layouts/base.astro";
import Icon from "#src/assets/icon.svg";
---
<Base>
  <main class="select-none max-w-full max-h-full overflow-hidden">
    <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold font-serif text-title text-center">
      Let's share!
      <div class="h-0.5 w-18 bg-accent mx-auto my-4"></div>
    </h1>
    <p class="text-text block text-center mt-8 max-w-full w-4xl mx-auto">
      <b>van den Hurk</b> is a common Dutch last name. It happens to be my last name. 
      That's why I bought <code class="py-1 px-1.5 rounded-md bg-background-1">hurk.dev</code>, 
      so that I could have 
      <a href="https://tygo.van.den.hurk.dev" class="text-accent hover:underline"
        ><code class="py-1 px-1.5 rounded-md bg-background-1"
          >tygo.van.den.hurk.dev</code></a>
      if your last name is <b>van den Hurk</b> and you want to have a subdomain, 
      they can be rented! The price is shared among all of us. The more there are,
      the cheaper this gets.
    </p>
    <p class="text-text block mt-4 max-w-full w-4xl mx-auto text-justify">
      the only reason I'm asking for money is because I have to pay for the domain 
      myself. By renting a subdomain you will be reducing the costs I pay yearly for
      renting this domain myself. As domains can be owned for a yearly fee. That's it.
      I'm not doing this to make a profit. The more of us renting it, the <b>lower</b>
      the price gets. if you are interested, feel free to
      <a href="https://redirects.tygo.van.den.hurk.dev/contact" class="text-accent hover:underline"
      >contact me</a>!
    </p>
    <Icon class="w-40 h-40 mx-auto my-16" />
  </main>
</Base>
